ndustries, Inc. designs, produces, and retails factory-built homes primarily in the United States. It operates in two segments: Factory-Built Housing and Financial Services. The company produces park model RVs; vacation cabins; and factory-built commercial structures, including apartment buildings, condominiums, hotels, workforce housing, schools, and housing for the United States military troops. It also produces various modular homes, which include single and multi-section ranch, split-level, and Cape Cod style homes, as well as two- and three-story homes, and multi-family units. In addition, the company provides conforming and non-conforming mortgages and home-only loans to purchasers of various brands of factory-built homes sold by company-owned retail stores, as well as various independent distributors, builders, communities, and developers. Further, it offers property and casualty insurance to owners of manufactured housing industry. The company distributes its products through a network of independent and company-owned retailers, planned community operators, and residential developers. The company was founded in 1965 and is headquartered in Phoenix, Arizona.","ceo_bio":"Mr. William C. Boor C.F.A. | President, CEO & Director | Age 59 | Compensation: $3.2M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 7K people. Revenue per employee of $291K ranks in the below the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers, with revenue growing 11%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $30K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 11\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Cavco Industries, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $4.9B market cap on $2.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +2% over the past three years and +12% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 23% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 13-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, and 22% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $232M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 10 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.40\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.3% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries a 76% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.7567643479074995},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $4.4M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Liquidity Mapping Around (CVCO) Price Events","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/101/Liquidity_Mapping_Around_CVCO_Price_Events_111026033002_1794342602.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794342602.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Comparing Installed Building Products (NYSE:IBP) and Cavco Industries (NASDAQ:CVCO)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/10/comparing-installed-building-products-nyseibp-and-cavco-industries-nasdaqcvco.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794315537.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.909,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Cavco Industries (CVCO) Could Be 10% Undervalued After Solid Second Quarter Earnings","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/consumer-durables/nasdaq-cvco/cavco-industries/news/cavco-industries-cvco-could-be-10-undervalued-after-solid-se","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793968239.233,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.972,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Cavco (CVCO) Is Up 15.86% in One Week: What You Should Know","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3023260/cavco-cvco-is-up-15-86-in-one-week-what-you-should-know?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_10-3023260","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":